    "summary": "Restored intel-core-fixes-001's snapshot (2309421), which changed nothing outside the owned paths. P1: step.ts replaces defer/flushPending with one sighting accumulator per player per step. The pending types (at a boundary), losses, journal replacements and targeted requests all add to it, and a new pass 4 makes one decision per player: uncapped, one message lists the types in type order with sectors drawn at send time, and requests are answered 'sighting'; capped, the free types become the one pending set and requests are answered 'capped' (a paid type is never queued). P2: a new startLead points only at sources or caches of any missing type, and otherwise sends a no-lead; a start never becomes a sighting. PendingSightingType.reason is narrowed to fresh|replacement. Added 6 scripted tests for finding 1 and one start test for the carried-only / late-joiner case. The property checker now allows one sighting message per player per step and checks every free trigger (a loss or a stale rumor) that needs a sighting: it must be in that step's message or in the pending set, and may wait only if the player was capped or the older snapshot can't answer it. Added property scenario 'quick, alpha, seed 15' so EXERCISED still reaches sighting:several-types. Updated docs/intel.md. Ran npm ci, then npm run typecheck, test:unit (580 passed), test:integration (36 passed) and build: all exit 0. All 10 changed or new scripted tests fail against the old step.ts and pass against the new one.",
